{
 "yae20f481ac2": {
  "row": 0,
  "sub": 3,
  "lines": [],
  "add": "- **\"Hindu\" for the people of Hind:** of the usual options first used by the **Arabs** (al-Hind, Hindu); the word itself is the Persian form of Sindhu (\"Hidu\" in Achaemenid inscriptions); Greeks said \"Indoi\", Chinese \"Shendu/Yindu\"."
 },
 "yf6803105d1a": {
  "row": 1,
  "sub": 6,
  "lines": [
   "6:4.0"
  ]
 },
 "n784d3a9977d": {
