 "y14febffe058": {
  "row": 3,
  "sub": 3,
  "lines": [],
  "add": "- **Disposal of the dead (Neolithic–Chalcolithic Andhra):** adults in **extended burials**, often with pots; children in urns – not cremation or mound burials."
 },
 "y59815d67260": {
  "row": 3,
  "sub": 3,
  "lines": [
   "3:0.2"
  ],
  "add": "- **Utnur ash mounds:** formed by repeatedly **burning cow dung inside wooden cattle stockades** rebuilt many times (Allchin) → proof of Neolithic **animal domestication**."
 },
 "yc9b3baedc93": {
  "row": 3,
  "sub": 2,
  "lines": [
   "2:1"
  ],
  "add": "- **Raw material:** South Indian Mesolithic microliths were mostly of **milky quartz**; found at **Nagarjunakonda** and **Renigunta**, among others."
 },
