  "row": 30,
  "sub": 1,
  "lines": [],
  "add": "- **Kanaganahalli** (Bhima river, **Kalaburagi**, Karnataka): Buddhist stupa site excavated by the **ASI, 1994–2001**; 1st–3rd c. CE stupa with the only inscribed stone portrait of **Ashoka** (\"Raya Asoko\"); now under ASI conservation."
 },
 "nac44caeceea": {
  "row": 31,
  "sub": 2,
  "lines": [
   "2:0"
  ],
  "add": "- **Why the heterodox sects arose:** the Vedic religion in **Sanskrit** was beyond common people; costly **yajnas** and animal sacrifice consumed the cattle needed for iron-plough farming; **Kshatriyas** resented Brahmin dominance (Mahavira and the Buddha were Kshatriyas); newly rich **Vaishyas** sought higher status and backed the new sects, not Vedic sacrifice."
 },
